{"skill":{"slug":"qwen-image","displayName":"Qwen Image"},"version":{"version":"1.0.0","createdAt":1770348338231,"changelog":"- Initial release of the qwen-image skill.\n- Generates high-quality AI images using the Alibaba Cloud Qwen Image API (DashScope).\n- Supports both Chinese and English text prompts.\n- Provides various image sizes and advanced options such as negative prompts and watermarking.\n- Returns image URLs for easy viewing; local saving is available by request.\n- Automatic extraction and markdown rendering of images from script output.","changelogSource":"auto","license":null,"files":[{"path":"SKILL.md","size":2873,"sha256":"36265ab3f43e3d9b9e4c99a7b4554979ea40744b7b337bc4b8d328deb2fe0877","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"scripts/generate_image.py","size":6648,"sha256":"d6cc92b11a74653730e46508dc872969a117aa5dec55aca8f9aab474d9084200","contentType":"text/plain"},{"path":"skill-card.md","size":2351,"sha256":"4e62c7fff9e18ef819863af1d2854e6b7dea8d16190a635f9c2d7247ada6e45e","contentType":"text/markdown"}],"security":{"status":"suspicious","hasWarnings":true,"checkedAt":1789036322614,"model":null,"hasScanResult":true,"sha256hash":"dc6f8b2b8c975b001fcc10580412f94a68ad2151218c0e1686f98a6d7ff8e8a1","virustotalUrl":"https://www.virustotal.com/gui/file/dc6f8b2b8c975b001fcc10580412f94a68ad2151218c0e1686f98a6d7ff8e8a1","scanners":{"vt":{"status":"suspicious","verdict":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","analysis":"Type: OpenClaw Skill\nName: qwen-image\nVersion: 1.0.0\n\nThe skill is generally benign, performing image generation via the Alibaba Cloud DashScope API as described. However, the `scripts/generate_image.py` file includes a `--no-verify-ssl` flag which, when enabled, disables SSL certificate verification for both the API request and image download. While the `SKILL.md` documentation mentions this as a feature for corporate proxies, disabling SSL verification is a high-risk capability that could expose the agent to Man-in-the-Middle attacks, making the skill suspicious despite the lack of clear malicious intent.","source":"palm","checkedAt":1779161769777},"skillspector":{"status":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","score":100,"severity":"CRITICAL","recommendation":"DO_NOT_INSTALL","issueCount":9,"checkedAt":1789036322614},"llm":{"status":"suspicious","verdict":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","confidence":"high","summary":"The skill does perform its stated Qwen image-generation job, but it handles paid API credentials in ways that can expose them.","dimensions":[{"detail":"Network access and a DashScope credential are proportionate for this provider skill, but local secret lookup guidance, command-line key use, optional TLS verification bypass for downloads, and unvalidated API-returned image URLs create avoidable exposure.","label":"Credentials","name":"environment_proportionality","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"The metadata declares uv as the required install tool via Homebrew; the script relies on uv runtime dependency resolution with an open-ended requests dependency.","label":"Install Mechanism","name":"install_mechanism","rating":"note"},{"detail":"The instructions tell agents to obtain API keys from local OpenClaw config paths or the environment, and examples pass the key on the command line without warning about shell history, logs, or process-argument exposure.","label":"Instruction Scope","name":"instruction_scope","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"No artifact-backed evidence shows persistence, autorun hooks, memory poisoning, privilege escalation, destructive behavior, or tool hijacking.","label":"Persistence & Privilege","name":"persistence_privilege","rating":"ok"},{"detail":"The image-generation purpose matches the main behavior: it sends the user prompt and bearer token to Alibaba Cloud DashScope and returns or downloads the generated image.","label":"Purpose & Capability","name":"purpose_capability","rating":"note"}],"guidance":"Install only if you intend to use Alibaba Cloud DashScope/Qwen Image and are comfortable sending prompts to that service. Prefer DASHSCOPE_API_KEY or a protected secret store over --api-key, avoid exposing keys in logs or command history, and avoid --no-verify-ssl unless you understand the download-integrity risk.","findings":"[PE3] expected: Downgraded: the script reads only an explicit API key argument or DASHSCOPE_API_KEY, not broad credential files; credential use is expected for DashScope access.\n[LP3] unexpected: Accepted as a concern because the skill needs network and credential access but does not clearly constrain or warn about how agents should access local secrets.\n[SQP-1] unexpected: Accepted as a minor routing concern: the description may activate for general image generation, not only explicit DashScope/Qwen use.\n[SQP-2] unexpected: Accepted: the API key is purpose-aligned, but retrieving it from local config and passing it via command-line examples is under-disclosed and risky.\n[SQP-3] expected: Downgraded: the Chinese default negative prompt is a product/locale quality choice, not evidence of malicious behavior.\n[SDI-4] unexpected: Partially accepted: the --no-verify-ssl option is documented broadly but only affects image downloads, which is confusing and weakens download integrity.\n[E1] expected: Downgraded: posting prompts and the bearer token to the documented DashScope endpoint is necessary for the advertised image-generation function.\n[TT2] unexpected: Accepted as a bounded concern: when saving locally, the script fetches an API-returned image URL without scheme or host validation.\n[T09] unexpected: Accepted for API key exposure through documented command-line usage.\n[T08] expected: Downgraded to a low-risk note: requests is a legitimate dependency, though the open-ended version range reduces reproducibility.","agenticRiskFindings":null,"riskSummary":null,"model":null,"checkedAt":1789036322614}}}}}